0000:                   ********************************************************************
0000:                   * Disasm - 6809/6309 disassembler
0000:                   *
0000:                   * $Id$
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Disasm v1.5 (c) 1988 by Ron Lammardo
0000:                   * 6309 additions by L. Curtis Boyle Jan. 1993
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
0000:                   * Comment
0000:                   * ------------------------------------------------------------------
0000:                   *   2      1987/03/12  Ron Lammardo
0000:                   * Added code for line,address,obj display added options 'o' and 'x'.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   3      1987/04/02  Ron Lammardo
0000:                   * Added code to provide commented disassembly of device descriptors.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   4      1987/11/16  Ron Lammardo
0000:                   * Fixed restart link failure, added code to display direct page addresses.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   5      1988/02/22  Ron Lammardo
0000:                   * Added code to display dp/u offsets; added code to display fcb bytes
0000:                   * preceding eom; added code for z option (hex input disassembly); 
0000:                   * added code to display date/time run
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/01/23  L. Curtis Boyle
0000:                   * Added code to handle 6309 instruction set additions
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2003/04/22  Rodney V. Hamilton
0000:                   * Added 4-digit year output.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2003/07/09  Rodney V. Hamilton
0000:                   * Changed output format of 6309 Bit commands.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2003/08/14  Rodney V. Hamilton
0000:                   * Added code to output "end" line
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2004/03/11  Rodney V. Hamilton
0000:                   * Updated TFM register selection
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2004/07/15  Robert Gault
0000:                   * Added code to indicate manual start and end for disassembly.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2004/08/08  Robert Gault
0000:                   * Changed getbyte routine to make "in memory" and disk i/o synchronize.
0000:                   * This also required a slight change to gotmod. Added testing so that manual
0000:                   * end/stop can't exceed module length. Almost have L lables working in Label
0000:                   * field. If there should be lables and you don't see them, use the s option
0000:                   * with s$0004$length_of_module. Then you should be able to use any values
0000:                   * for start/stop and the L labels will still be present.
0000:                   * Change in z option required by change in getbyte.
0000:                   * S option uses fake data size. Added minor changes suggested by R.V.H.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *         2005/10/13  Robert Gault
0000:                   * Forced to shrink labeltab size so that os9boot could be disassembled.
0000:                   
0000:                            nam   Disasm
0000:                            ttl   6809/6309 disassembler
0000:                   
0000:                            ifp1
0000:                            use   defsfile
0000:                            endc
0000:                   
0011:                   typ      set   Prgrm+Objct
0080:                   attrev   set   ReEnt+revision
0000:                   revision set   $00
0005:                   edtn     set   5 edition
0035:                   edition  equ   $30+edtn ascii edition
0000:                   
0000: 87CD2AF6000D1180           mod   eom,mname,typ,attrev,start,datend
0009: 1AF82000
0000:                   
0000:                   pcrzero  equ   *-$0D module start
