08CC:                   **  1 byte op code table               **
08CC:                   *****************************************
08CC:                   * Position in table is opcode, byte stored there is how to interpret it
08CC:                   * Interpreter bytes are:
08CC:                   * $FF: Direct page mode (1 byte address)
08CC:                   * $FE: FCB (unknown single byte)
08CC:                   * $FD: Implied (single byte by itself)
08CC:                   * $FC: 2 byte relative
08CC:                   * $FB: 1 byte immediate
08CC:                   * $FA: Dual register (EXG/TFR)
08CC:                   * $F9: 1 byte relative
08CC:                   * $F8: Indexed (1 or more post bytes)
08CC:                   * $F7: Stack (PSH/PUL) register post-byte
08CC:                   * $F6: ??? (internal use?)
08CC:                   * $F5: SWI???
08CC:                   * $F4: Extended (2 byte address)
08CC:                   * $F3: 2 byte immediate
08CC:                   * $F2: 4 byte immediate
08CC:                   * $F1: In memory (AIM, etc.)
08CC:                   * $F0: Bit commands (LDBT, etc.)
